[size=6][b]Concentration Redux[/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Dual-Stance Spellcasting Architecture for Baldur's Gate 3 (Patch 7 & Patch 8)[/i][/size]

[line]

[size=4][b]✦ The Problem in Vanilla 5e[/b][/size]
In D&D 5e and vanilla Baldur's Gate 3, nearly every worthwhile spell competes for a single, restrictive concentration slot:
[list]
[*]Casting an iconic staple like [i]Bless[/i] or [i]Shield of Faith[/i] completely locks your caster out of using [i]Spirit Guardians[/i], [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Call Lightning[/i], or [i]Hold Person[/i].
[*]Buffs vanish from a single stray 1-damage surface tick or an off-screen archer.
[*]Outside turn-based combat, 10-turn (60-second) timers expire while looting chests or reading dialogue.
[/list]

[size=4][b]✦ The Redesign: Three Tactical Stances[/b][/size]
Concentration Redux splits spellcasting focus into two distinct, congruent cognitive layers:

[size=4][color=#ffd700][b]1. Pure Support (Solo Focus)[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Condition:[/b] Only maintaining a Focus buff ([i]Bless[/i], [i]Shield of Faith[/i], [i]Heroism[/i], [i]Haste[/i], etc.).
[*][b]Defensive Resilience:[/b] [b]100% Unbreakable by Damage.[/b] No Constitution saving throws required against damage ticks, DoTs, or environmental surfaces.
[*][b]Duration:[/b] Indefinite until Long Rest or manual dismissal.
[*][b]Allowed Actions:[/b] All weapon attacks, spells, and abilities permitted.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#87cefa][b]2. Dedicated Juggernaut (Solo Concentration)[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Condition:[/b] Only maintaining an active combat conduit ([i]Spirit Guardians[/i], [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Fog Cloud[/i], [i]Moonbeam[/i], [i]Hold Person[/i], etc.).
[*][b]Defensive Resilience:[/b] Runs in the native engine slot with standard Constitution saving throws. Benefits from [b]War Caster[/b] Advantage.
[*][b]Allowed Actions:[/b] Whitelisted tactical actions ([i]Dash[/i], [i]Disengage[/i], [i]Shove[/i], [i]Throw[/i], [i]Jump[/i], etc.). Weapon attacks are permitted for martial domains ([i]War[/i] & [i]Tempest[/i]). Casting unauthorized spells breaks the conduit.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#da70d6][b]3. The Overclock (Both Active Simultaneously)[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Condition:[/b] Caster is actively maintaining both Focus AND Concentration at the same time.
[*][b]Defensive Resilience:[/b] Pushes your caster's mental bandwidth to the absolute limit. When taking damage:
[list]
[*]The native Concentration conduit rolls standard saves (with War Caster if proficient).
[*]Focus independently rolls a Constitution saving throw [b]with Advantage[/b] (2d20, pick highest)!
[/list]
[*][b]Graceful Fallback:[/b] If your combat conduit drops or is dismissed, Focus seamlessly drops back into unbreakable solo mode!
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]✦ Spell Classifications[/b][/size]

[b]1. Focus (Indefinite Duration Buffs)[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Combat & Defensive Wards:[/b] [i]Bless[/i], [i]Shield of Faith[/i], [i]Heroism[/i], [i]Protection from Evil and Good[/i], [i]Barkskin[/i], [i]Stoneskin[/i], [i]Shield of Thralls[/i]
[*][b]Single-Target Marks:[/b] [i]Hunter's Mark[/i], [i]Hex[/i], [i]Bane[/i], [i]Bestow Curse[/i]
[*][b]Physical Augmentations:[/b] [i]Haste[/i], [i]Enlarge/Reduce[/i], [i]Fly[/i], [i]Expeditious Retreat[/i], [i]Blur[/i], [i]Magic Weapon[/i], [i]Elemental Weapon[/i]
[*][b]Stealth & Senses:[/b] [i]Invisibility[/i], [i]Greater Invisibility[/i], [i]Pass Without Trace[/i], [i]Detect Thoughts[/i]
[/list]
[i]Note: Focus buffs are mutually exclusive per caster. Casting a new Focus spell naturally replaces your current one.[/i]

[quote][b]Class Spells vs. Equipment & Scrolls:[/b]
Class investments (spellbook spells, Bard Magical Secrets, multiclassing, Magic Initiate feats) utilize the full Focus system.
Spells granted by bound equipment (e.g. Whispering Promise, Darkfire Shortbow) and consumable scrolls intentionally follow vanilla rules (10-turn limit, standard damage saves) to prevent item abuse.[/quote]

[b]2. Concentration (Combat Stances & Conduits)[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Emanations & Auras:[/b] [i]Spirit Guardians[/i] (Radiant / Necrotic), [i]Aura of Vitality[/i], [i]Crusader's Mantle[/i], [i]Holy Aura[/i]
[*][b]Sustained Beams & Activations:[/b] [i]Call Lightning[/i], [i]Moonbeam[/i], [i]Witch Bolt[/i], [i]Heat Metal[/i], [i]Sunbeam[/i], [i]Eyebite[/i], [i]Telekinesis[/i]
[*][b]Hazard Anchors:[/b] [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Darkness[/i], [i]Cloud of Daggers[/i], [i]Fog Cloud[/i], [i]Silence[/i], [i]Spike Growth[/i], [i]Sleet Storm[/i], [i]Hunger of Hadar[/i], [i]Cloudkill[/i], [i]Evard's Black Tentacles[/i], [i]Insect Plague[/i]
[*][b]Hard Crowd Control:[/b] [i]Hold Person[/i], [i]Hold Monster[/i], [i]Hypnotic Pattern[/i], [i]Banishment[/i], [i]Tasha's Hideous Laughter[/i], [i]Slow[/i], [i]Confusion[/i], [i]Otiluke's Resilient Sphere[/i]
[/list]

[b]3. Reapplication Spells (Hex & Hunter's Mark)[/b]
[list]
[*]When your marked target dies, the corpse target is cleanly detached from tracking while preserving Focus on the caster.
[*]The free [i]Reapply[/i] abilities remain on your hotbar and are fully whitelisted—re-marking a new foe will never break active Concentration.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]✦ UI, Dismissal & Visual Clarity[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Side-by-Side Portrait Badges:[/b] Both conditions display clearly in the character's portrait tray:
[list]
[*]Radiant Sun icon for [b]Focus[/b]
[*]Purple Mind Conduit icon for [b]Concentration[/b]
[/list]
[*][b]Dismissing Focus:[/b] While maintaining Focus, the caster gains a free, 0-action [b]Dismiss Focus[/b] ability on their hotbar to cancel it on demand.
[*][b]Dismissing Concentration:[/b] Uses Baldur's Gate 3's [b]native 'X' button[/b] directly beneath the portrait HUD (or by casting another conduit).
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]✦ Tactical Synergies & Balance Rules[/b][/size]

[b]Combat Channeling Perk[/b]
War Domain and Tempest Domain Clerics receive the [b]Combat Channeling[/b] perk at Level 1:
[list]
[*]Execute melee and ranged weapon attacks, leverage Extra Attack, and trigger special weapon actions ([i]Lacerate[/i], [i]Topple[/i], [i]Flourish[/i], [i]Cleave[/i], [i]Pommel Strike[/i], etc.) without breaking active Concentration.
[*]Script Extender dynamically inspects weapon action properties to support modded martial actions and weapon masteries.
[*]Non-combat domains attempting unauthorized physical attacks will shatter their active channel.
[/list]

[b]War Caster Feat Integration[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Without War Caster:[/b] Focus rolls with Advantage during Overclock; Channeling rolls a standard 1d20 save.
[*][b]With War Caster:[/b] Grants Advantage to Channeling saves. Because Focus already rolls with Advantage, [b]War Caster ensures BOTH saves have Advantage during Overclock![/b]
[*][b]Reactive Spellcasting:[/b] Casting [i]Shocking Grasp[/i] as an Opportunity Attack reaction via War Caster is fully permitted and will not break your active channel.
[/list]

[b]Strict Reaction Spells[/b]
[list]
[*]Casting emergency spell reactions ([i]Shield[/i], [i]Counterspell[/i], [i]Hellish Rebuke[/i]) immediately shatters active combat conduits.
[*]Tooltips and reaction cards feature clear [b]Concentration Disruption[/b] warnings.
[*]Keep "Ask" enabled in your Reactions tab ([i]K[/i]) so you can deliberately choose when to trade your channel in life-or-death situations.
[/list]

[b]Loss of Control (5e Compliance)[/b]
If a caster is afflicted with hard incapacitation ([i]Stunned[/i], [i]Paralyzed[/i], [i]Petrified[/i], [i]Sleep[/i], [i]Unconscious[/i], [i]Downed[/i], [i]Dead[/i]), Focus and all linked buffs immediately drop.

[line]

[size=4][b]✦ Requirements & Installation[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Game Version:[/b] Baldur's Gate 3 ([b]Patch 7 / Patch 8+[/b])
[*][b]Required Mod:[/b] [url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se/releases]Baldur's Gate 3 Script Extender (BG3SE)[/url] (v32 or newer recommended)
[/list]

[b]Installation via Vortex or BG3 Mod Manager:[/b]
[olist]
[*]Download the `.zip` archive from the Files tab.
[*]Import and install via [b]Vortex[/b] or [b]BG3 Mod Manager[/b].
[*]Enable [b]Concentration Redux[/b] in your active load order and export.
[*]Safe to install on existing playthroughs!
[/olist]
